    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Envo Blocks adds two things to the block editor: a template library with JSON import and export, and a set of WooCommerce blocks for product pages, the cart and landing pages that WordPress and WooCommerce do not have.</p>\n<h4>Templates Import and Export</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>Templates Import</strong> button in the editor header opens a library of page templates, with categories and search.</li>\n<li><strong>Export as JSON</strong> in the editor options menu saves the current page as a JSON file, so you can move it to another site.</li>\n<li>Every imported template is checked: only blocks that exist on your site are used and all content is sanitized.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>WooCommerce blocks</h4>\n<p>All blocks are in their own <strong>Envo Blocks</strong> section of the block inserter.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Trust Badges</strong> – payment method icons (Visa, Mastercard, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Klarna and more) and short guarantees such as &#8220;Secure payment&#8221; or &#8220;30-day returns&#8221;.</li>\n<li><strong>Features Bar</strong> – a row of shop benefits with icons: free shipping, easy returns, support, secure payment. Columns for desktop and mobile, three icon styles, optional links.</li>\n<li><strong>Coupon Code Box</strong> – shows a WooCommerce coupon with a &#8220;Copy code&#8221; button and an optional &#8220;Apply to cart&#8221; button. The discount, the minimum order amount and the expiry date are read from the coupon, and the box hides itself when the coupon expires.</li>\n<li><strong>Delivery Estimate</strong> – &#8220;Order within 2 h 15 min and we ship it today&#8221; with the estimated delivery date. Uses your cut-off time, shipping days, carrier delivery days and holidays, and is recalculated in the browser, so it stays correct on cached pages.</li>\n<li><strong>Rating Summary</strong> – the average rating and a 5★ to 1★ breakdown of the reviews, for the current product, a chosen product or the whole shop.</li>\n<li><strong>Recently Viewed Products</strong> – products the visitor looked at last. The list is kept in the visitor&#8217;s browser (no cookies, nothing stored on the server) and loaded from the WooCommerce Store API, so it works with page caching.</li>\n<li><strong>Size Guide</strong> – a link or button that opens your size chart in a pop-up window. The window content is made of normal blocks, so you can use tables, images and text.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every block has color settings and works with the spacing and typography settings of your theme. Trust Badges, Features Bar, Delivery Estimate and Size Guide also work without WooCommerce.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the <code>envo-blocks</code> folder to <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>, or install the plugin from Plugins &gt; Add New.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Open a page in the block editor: use the <strong>Templates Import</strong> button in the header, or find the blocks in the <strong>Envo Blocks</strong> section of the inserter.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>WooCommerce must be active for the Coupon Code Box, Rating Summary and Recently Viewed Products blocks.</p>\n",
        "faq": "\n<h4>\nDoes the plugin need WooCommerce?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The template import and export, Trust Badges, Features Bar, Delivery Estimate and Size Guide work without it. Coupon Code Box, Rating Summary and Recently Viewed Products are available only when WooCommerce is active.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nDoes the plugin connect to external services?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. The plugin does not send any data to external servers. The Coupon Code Box (&#8220;Apply to cart&#8221;) and the Recently Viewed Products block use the WooCommerce Store API of your own site. The &#8220;Preview&#8221; links of the templates open demo pages in a new tab only when you click them.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nWhere does Recently Viewed Products keep the history?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>In the visitor&#8217;s browser (localStorage), up to the last 24 product IDs. Nothing is saved on the server and no cookie is set. Visitors can clear the history with the optional &#8220;Clear history&#8221; link.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nIn which time zone does the Delivery Estimate count?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>In the time zone set in Settings &gt; General. Holidays are entered as <code>2026-12-24</code> for one day or <code>12-25</code> for every year.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nAre the payment icons official logos?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No. They are simplified marks drawn for this plugin so that visitors recognise the payment methods. All trademarks belong to their owners.</p>\n</p>\n<h4>\nCan I translate the plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. The plugin is fully translatable, including the block editor settings. Translations are managed on translate.wordpress.org; a POT file is included in the <code>languages</code> folder.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>New: Envo Blocks section in the block inserter.</li>\n<li>New: Trust Badges, Features Bar, Coupon Code Box, Delivery Estimate, Rating Summary, Recently Viewed Products and Size Guide blocks.</li>\n<li>New: Online Store Home, Sale Landing Page and About Our Store templates.</li>\n<li>Improved: template text alignment works in WordPress 7.0 and newer.</li>\n<li>Improved: all texts are translatable, POT file added.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>First release: Templates Import button and Export as JSON.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Import ready-made page templates, export pages as JSON and add WooCommerce blocks: trust badges, coupon box, delivery estimate, size guide and more.",
    "description": "<p>Envo Blocks adds two things to the block editor: a template library with JSON import and export, and a set of WooCommerce blocks for product pages, the cart and landing pages that WordPress and WooCommerce do not have.</p>\n<h4>Templates Import and Export</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>Templates Import</strong> button in the editor header opens a library of page templates, with categories and search.</li>\n<li><strong>Export as JSON</strong> in the editor options menu saves the current page as a JSON file, so you can move it to another site.</li>\n<li>Every imported template is checked: only blocks that exist on your site are used and all content is sanitized.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>WooCommerce blocks</h4>\n<p>All blocks are in their own <strong>Envo Blocks</strong> section of the block inserter.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Trust Badges</strong> – payment method icons (Visa, Mastercard, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay, Klarna and more) and short guarantees such as &#8220;Secure payment&#8221; or &#8220;30-day returns&#8221;.</li>\n<li><strong>Features Bar</strong> – a row of shop benefits with icons: free shipping, easy returns, support, secure payment. Columns for desktop and mobile, three icon styles, optional links.</li>\n<li><strong>Coupon Code Box</strong> – shows a WooCommerce coupon with a &#8220;Copy code&#8221; button and an optional &#8220;Apply to cart&#8221; button. The discount, the minimum order amount and the expiry date are read from the coupon, and the box hides itself when the coupon expires.</li>\n<li><strong>Delivery Estimate</strong> – &#8220;Order within 2 h 15 min and we ship it today&#8221; with the estimated delivery date. Uses your cut-off time, shipping days, carrier delivery days and holidays, and is recalculated in the browser, so it stays correct on cached pages.</li>\n<li><strong>Rating Summary</strong> – the average rating and a 5★ to 1★ breakdown of the reviews, for the current product, a chosen product or the whole shop.</li>\n<li><strong>Recently Viewed Products</strong> – products the visitor looked at last. The list is kept in the visitor&#8217;s browser (no cookies, nothing stored on the server) and loaded from the WooCommerce Store API, so it works with page caching.</li>\n<li><strong>Size Guide</strong> – a link or button that opens your size chart in a pop-up window. The window content is made of normal blocks, so you can use tables, images and text.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every block has color settings and works with the spacing and typography settings of your theme. Trust Badges, Features Bar, Delivery Estimate and Size Guide also work without WooCommerce.</p>\n",
